  "clinical_uncertainties": [],
  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It's only small, but my hands have been shaky. When I'm holding a cup of tea the saucer rattles, and it's embarrassing in front of company.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:02",
      "end_timestamp": "01:16",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Shaky hands, and it's worst when you're holding something up. How long has that been going on?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:19",
      "end_timestamp": "01:29",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Two months, I'd say, give or take. It crept in, I didn't notice it at first, then my neighbour said it to me over the fence.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:31",
      "end_timestamp": "01:44",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Well, there's cramps in my calves at night. They wake me up, and I have to get out of bed and walk it off on the cold floor.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:53",
      "end_timestamp": "02:06",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Does that happen every night, or just now and then?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:09",
      "end_timestamp": "02:15",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "A few nights a week. My sister's dog does the same thing in her sleep, kicking away, so maybe it's catching.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:17",
      "end_timestamp": "02:29",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll leave the dog out of the diagnosis. Let me ask a few things that matter in your situation. Any fever lately, or any burning when you pass water?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:31",
      "end_timestamp": "02:45",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]",
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, none of that. No fever, and the water is grand, nothing stinging.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:48",
      "end_timestamp": "02:56",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]",
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good, that's what I wanted to hear. I know it's years ago now, but how long has it been since your kidney transplant?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:59",
      "end_timestamp": "03:12",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Four years ago this March. I still call it my second birthday, and my family bring a cake every year.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:13",
      "end_timestamp": "03:25",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Lovely tradition. And you're on tacrolimus for that, is that right? What dose?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:27",
      "end_timestamp": "03:33",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "The tacrolimus, 3 mg twice a day, morning and evening. I never miss it, I've it set on the phone, and the pharmacist gives out to me if I'm late for the refill.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:35",
      "end_timestamp": "03:51",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Your blood pressure is 132 over 78, which is very respectable. And on the scales you're 74 kg, the same as last time within a pound or so.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:30",
      "end_timestamp": "04:45",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Now hold both arms out in front of you, fingers spread, as if you were carrying a tray. There, I can see a fine tremor in both outstretched hands, quite fine and regular.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:07",
      "end_timestamp": "05:25",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Your neighbour is not a neurologist, thankfully. Let me explain my thinking. What I think this is, most likely, is a side effect of the tacrolimus. It's a known thing with that tablet, and it shows up as a fine shake in the hands.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:36",
      "end_timestamp": "05:59",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "No chance. Cutting back on caffeine may help the shaking a little, and holding the cup with both hands for now is no shame.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:05",
      "end_timestamp": "07:18",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Exactly. If the shaking gets worse over the next few weeks, or the cramps start to keep you up every night, ring the clinic and ask for me.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:28",
      "end_timestamp": "07:43",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
    }
  ],
